are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/joined(separator:)":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"title":"joined(separator:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"joined","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Separator","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"separator","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Separator"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s14JoinedSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"JoinedSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/joined(separator:)","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/joined(separator:)","role":"symbol"}}}